{
  "id": "add-binary",
  "questionId": "add-binary",
  "slug": "add-binary",
  "title": "Add Binary",
  "difficulty": "Easy",
  "category": "Greedy",
  "patterns": [
    "greedy",
    "simulation",
    "bit manipulation"
  ],
  "lists": [
    "grind-75",
    "interview-150"
  ],
  "hints": [
    "these strings can be up to 10^4 characters long - far too long to convert to a native integer type, so you need to add them digit by digit like you would on paper",
    "walk both strings from the rightmost character toward the left, maintaining a running carry",
    "at each position, sum the two bits (using 0 if a position runs past the start of the shorter string) plus the carry, the result bit is that sum mod 2 and the new carry is that sum divided by 2",
    "after the last position, if a carry remains, prepend an extra '1' to the result",
    "build the result from least significant to most significant bit, then reverse it before returning (or prepend at each step)"
  ],
  "commonMistakes": [
    "assuming both strings are the same length and not handling the shorter one running out of digits first",
    "forgetting to flush a leftover carry after processing the longest string, dropping a leading 1",
    "converting to a native integer type, which overflows for the 10^4-length constraint",
    "building the result in the wrong order and forgetting to reverse it"
  ],
  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You're given two binary strings `a` and `b`, each made up of only the characters '0' and '1', with no leading zeroes unless the string is exactly \"0\".\n\n**Add them together as binary numbers and return the sum as a binary string, also with no leading zeroes.**\n",
    "constraints": [
      "1 <= length of a, length of b <= 10^4",
      "each character of a and b is '0' or '1'",
      "neither a nor b has leading zeroes, except the single string \"0\""
    ],
    "notes": [
      "both inputs are \"0\"",
      "the two strings have very different lengths",
      "the addition produces a carry out of the most significant bit, growing the result by one digit",
      "no carries occur anywhere (simple digit-by-digit sum)"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Arguments passed into solution function",
    "outputFormat": "Return output matching method signature",
    "sampleTestCases": [
